# Extracted assets (run ./extract_assets.sh or .\extract_assets.ps1 to generate)
Data/*
!Data/opcodes

# A profile is configuration, not an asset: the four JSONs an expansion is
# defined by are tracked, and everything else that lands in its directory is
# extracted and is not. The four existing profiles predate the Data/* rule and
# stayed tracked by being tracked already; a fifth needs saying.
!Data/expansions/
Data/expansions/*
!Data/expansions/*/
Data/expansions/*/*
!Data/expansions/*/expansion.json
!Data/expansions/*/opcodes.json
!Data/expansions/*/update_fields.json
!Data/expansions/*/dbc_layouts.json
!Data/expansions/*/movement_sequences.json

ingest/

# Asset archives dropped at the repo root rather than into ingest/. An MPQ is
# hundreds of megabytes and `git add -A` will take one without complaint.
*.MPQ
*.mpq

# Asset pipeline state and texture packs
asset_pipeline/

# Local texture dumps / extracted art should never be committed
assets/textures/
node_modules/

# Python cache artifacts
tools/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# World editor output: scaffolded/exported zones and per-user ImGui layout
custom_zones/
wowee_editor_layout.ini

#agents
AGENTS.md
codex-loop.sh

# The headless runner keeps its config here so it cannot overwrite the
# player's missing-API and Lua-error lists. One root per check that drives it,
# so a run cannot read a store some other check left: the runner loads the CVar
# store at start-up, and a shared root made a result depend on run order.
logs/*_config/

# Canary builds: deliberately broken binaries for watching a check fail.
# Kept out of build/ because that is what the player runs.
build-canary/

# Android Gradle build outputs
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/.cxx/
android/local.properties
